# MarketHunter Experiment 1 runtime - environment file example.
#
# Copy to:
# /home/ubuntu/MarketHunter/deploy/systemd/experiment1-runtime.env
# The real file is intentionally not committed. experiment1-runtime.service
# loads it through EnvironmentFile=-..., so a missing file remains harmless.

# Optional DB override (default is data/experiment1.db relative to repo root).
#EXPERIMENT1_DB_PATH=/home/ubuntu/MarketHunter/data/experiment1.db

# Optional GIL -> MarketHunter machine transport through the canonical Slack
# audit channel. It is OFF unless explicitly enabled. Ordinary Slack prose is
# never parsed; only an exact `GIL DECISION ENVELOPE v1` JSON block from the
# fixed canonical channel/user can enter the durable GIL Decision Inbox.
#
# Required Slack app/token capability when enabled:
# - read message history for #global-investment-lab (channels:history for the
#   current public channel shape; the app may also need to be a channel member,
#   depending on Slack token type/configuration).
# - read-only is sufficient; the runtime never posts to Slack.
#
# NEVER commit the real token.
#GIL_SLACK_TRANSPORT_ENABLED=1
#GIL_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-REDACTED
#GIL_SLACK_CHANNEL_ID=C0BNACTF4E4
#GIL_SLACK_ALLOWED_USER_ID=U0BMKMQ4U04
#GIL_SLACK_CHECKPOINT_PATH=/home/ubuntu/MarketHunter/data/experiment1_gil_slack_checkpoint.json
